{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"6b953230-6e19-4297-8569-9672d34f89db","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented proper prompt caching to prevent memory writes from invalidating static instructions.\n\n### Key Changes\n- **`build_system` in `bot.py`** now creates **two separate `ephemeral` cache segments**:\n  1. **Static instructions** – unchanged across all requests.\n  2. **Dynamic athlete context** – date, profile, zones, goals, facts, language.  \n  This mirrors the colleague’s solution of using two `cache_control` markers, ensuring only the dynamic tail is refreshed on `save_fact` calls.\n\n### Parts of the Note Utilized\n- Two `cache_control: {\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}` markers to split static and dynamic sections.  \n- Keeping the static block byte‑identical for all users.  \n- Leaving all long‑term facts in the dynamic tail (no top‑N filtering).  \n- Maintaining the existing tool selection logic unchanged.\n\n### Verification Steps\n1. Send two consecutive messages without updating facts – `cache_read_input_tokens` should cover the full prompt.  \n2. Call `save_fact` then send another message – `cache_read_input_tokens` should now cover only the static block, while `cache_creation_input_tokens` reflects only the dynamic tail (~240 tokens).\n\nThe modifications are in **[`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-8sl131/bot.py#L130-L138)** and detailed in **[`ANSWER.md`](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6b953230-6e19-4297-8569-9672d34f89db/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":53.353484,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":30372,"output_tokens":3467,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":163904,"total_tokens":33839}}}
